The first substantive concern is now concrete: several “observed” vectors are produced from copied protocol-label lists after only a broad success/read-only predicate, rather than from per-field seams. For example, the dry-run effect inventory and planning/repair pipelines are literal protocol taxonomies, and the private-build failure probe reports “no manager-home lock acquired” by inspecting lock state only after the operation has released it. I’m testing these as adversarial product-seam sabotages; a surviving sabotage would require changes rather than acceptance even though the 378 vector mutations are green.
