Two adversarial checks now survive exactly when they must fail:

- A deliberate manager-home lock acquisition during the second-build failure path occurred once, yet the observer still reported `manager_home_lock_acquired: false` and the entire normative case matched.
- Replacing CocoaSkills’ skill-validation gate with a no-op still produced the complete 11-gate planning vector and `build-eligible`.
- Replacing the repair audit gate with a no-op still produced the complete 10-stage repair pipeline and `rebuilt-and-journaled`.

That confirms the green scalar audit is vector-side mutation sensitivity, not full product-seam sensitivity. I’m still rerunning the advertised baseline gates so the verdict distinguishes “tests green” from “acceptance criteria actually met.”
